    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Four cousins Alan, Bob, Carl and Dan are 3, 8, 12 and 14 years old, although not necessarily in that order. Alan is younger than Carl. The sum of the ages of Alan and Dan is divisible by 5. The sum of the ages of Carl and Dan is divisible by 5. What is the sum of the ages of Alan and Bob?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "26"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "22"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "17"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "15"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "11"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the sums divisible by 5",
        "body": "Pair sums of $3,8,12,14$: only $3+12=15$ and $8+12=20$ are multiples of 5. Dan appears in both required sums, so Dan is 12, and Alan, Carl are 3 and 8. Alan is younger, so Alan is 3 and Carl is 8, leaving Bob as 14. Alan + Bob $=3+14=17$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 17**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
